This repository contains an orchestration layer for a connectome-inspired fruit-fly
brain. It links against, loads, or documents the following third-party work.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
flywire-fly-lab
  https://github.com/suifei/flywire-fly-lab
  License: Apache License, Version 2.0

  NOT VENDORED HERE. brain_b/b_loop/stage1_loop.js loads it at runtime:

      const REPO = process.env.FLYLAB || '/root/flywire-fly-lab';
      const { ConnectomeBrain } = require(path.join(REPO, 'dodge/brain.js'));

  You must obtain that project separately. The datasets under its results/
  directory are published under CC BY-NC 4.0 (non-commercial); they are not
  redistributed here and no rights to them are granted by this repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ESP-Mosaico Vibe
  https://github.com/esp-mosaico/esp-mosaico-vibe
  Board-side framework only. The board firmware lives in the sibling repository
  https://github.com/snownmouse/cyber-fly and is not part of this repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scientific basis (no code taken)

  - FlyWire consortium, "Neuronal wiring diagram of an adult brain",
    Nature 634 (2024).
  - Shiu, Sterne et al., "A Drosophila computational brain model reveals
    sensorimotor processing", Nature 634:210-219 (2024).

  This project is a functional realisation of the same principle
  (sensory input -> connectome computation -> motor output). It is not a
  per-neuron simulation of all ~140,000 cells.
